ref=e939] [cursor=pointer]:\n                      - img [ref=e941]\n                    - button \"Hide post by Marielle Mikson\" [ref=e943] [cursor=pointer]:\n                      - img [ref=e945]\n                  - paragraph [ref=e947]:\n                    - generic [ref=e948]:\n                      - text: Ever planned a holiday without choosing the destination, dates, or even packing? ✈️\n                      - text: Exactly. Chaos. Yet many of us treat our careers exactly like that.\n                      - text: Today I had the pleasure of joining a fantastic session with\n                      - link \"Emily Edwards ✈️\" [ref=e950] [cursor=pointer]:\n                        - /url: https://www.linkedin.com/in/emilyedwardscoaching/\n                        - strong [ref=e952]: Emily Edwards ✈️\n                      - text: \", where we started a 3-step journey, and step one was all about thinking BIG.\"\n                      - text: \"One thing that stuck with me: when we set goals, our brain releases dopamine, making it more likely that we’ll actually take action. In other words, dreaming big isn’t fluffy - it’s science. 🧠\"\n                      - text: \"Emily challenged us with three powerful questions:\"\n                      - text: 1️⃣ What do you want people to say about you at your retirement party?\n                      - text: What would you want your boss or colleagues to say about the impact you made?\n                      - text: 2️⃣ What is the universe asking from you?\n                      - text: Sometimes we get little signs about where we should go next. The question is… are we actually listening?\n                      - text: 3️⃣ What is your Ikigai?\n                      - text: That sweet spot between what you love, what you’re good at, what the world needs, and what you can be paid for.\n                      - text: We also talked about those moments when we feel we don’t deserve the next step. Those invisible blockers that quietly hold us back. Recognising them is the first step to removing them.\n                      - text: My step one? ✨ Ask the universe.\n                      - text: Thank you Emily, for such an inspiring and thought-provoking session today. Looking forward to the next one next week.\n                      - link \"#leadership\" [ref=e953] [cursor=pointer]:\n                        - /url: https://www.linkedin.com/search/results/all/?keywords=%23leadership&origin=HASH_TAG_FROM_FEED\n                        - strong [ref=e955]: \"#leadership\"\n                      - link \"#careerdevelopment\" [ref=e956] [cursor=pointer]:\n                        - /url: https://www.linkedin.com/search/results/all/?keywords=%23careerdevelopment&origin=HASH_TAG_FROM_FEED\n                        - strong [ref=e958]: \"#careerdevelopment\"\n                      - link \"#ikigai\" [ref=e959] [cursor=pointer]:\n                        - /url: https://www.linkedin.com/search/results/all/?keywords=%23ikigai&origin=HASH_TAG_FROM_FEED\n                        - strong [ref=e961]: \"#ikigai\"\n                      - link \"Emily Edwards Coaching\" [ref=e962] [cursor=pointer]:\n                        - /url: https://www.linkedin.com/company/emily-edwards-coaching/\n                        - strong [ref=e964]: Emily Edwards Coaching\n                      - button:\n                        - generic [ref=e966] [cursor=pointer]: … more\n                  - generic [ref=e967]:\n                    - link \"View image\" [ref=e968] [cursor=pointer]:\n                      - /url: https://www.linkedin.com/feed/\n                      - figure \"View image\" [ref=e969]:\n                        - img \"View image\" [ref=e970]\n                    - button \"This image has content credentials.\" [ref=e971] [cursor=pointer]:\n                      - figure [ref=e973]:\n                        - img [ref=e974]\n                  - generic [ref=e977]:\n                    - link \"4 reactio